          "url": "https://andersmurphy.com/2025/12/02/100000-tps-over-a-billion-rows-the-unreasonable-effectiveness-of-sqlite.html",
          "source": "Hacker News",
          "date": "2025-12-02T17:59:53Z",
          "language": "en",
          "section": "us_news",
          "raw_content": "SQLite doesn't have MVCC! It only has a single writer! SQLite is for phones and mobile apps (and the occasional airliner)! For web servers use a proper database like Postgres! In this article I'll go over why being embedded and a single writer are not deficiencies but actually allow SQLite to scale so unreasonably well. For the code examples I will be using Clojure. But, what they cover should be applicable to most programming language.",
